# Release Build Gate

When finishing a unit of work that would normally end in an Android/EAS build:

1. **Commit everything first.** Stage and commit all changes so the working tree
   is clean. Never leave dirty/uncommitted files before a build.
2. **Stop before building.** Do NOT auto-run the build scripts
   (`tools/release/BUILD_RELEASE_CANDIDATE.ps1`, `eas build`, gradle bundle, etc.)
   or bump the version code for a build on your own.
3. **Ask for explicit confirmation.** Tell the user the work is committed and ask
   them to confirm they're ready for a build — they may want to add more changes first.
4. Only after the user explicitly says to build should you bump the version code,
   run the pre-release regression gate, and produce the AAB.

This exists so the user can batch additional changes into a single build instead
of getting a fresh build after every change.
